# Manual annotated Markdown /2 draft synchronization

Scope: only `doc/migration/authored/21-doc-pages.nepld` was edited. Root-owned spec/API/code/registry remain untouched. No commit or canonical cutover was performed. This is author self-check; independent review and production parse/lower/render remain separate.

The source was fixed before authoring as `source.md`; its SHA256 is `03c74625aaac5d9023c70f58bf8316dd20ce800cad8fc2a764449e591b34f0a7`. Original draft SHA256 is `f0c7b1748fcce16d8f29786256a4f8cef80d6f7dc24ec6f4fe11c7da3308afb5`. Final draft SHA256 is `b6a0fe957adc6abeae3c3791e4f0fa7822a5184bdc08ba2e4cdf3eeaaf70ed1f`.

Manual changes have three locations, all in Section `annotated`:

1. Renderer becomes `nepl3-tools.markdown-annotated/2`; three sentences explain the added list/table capability, preserving prior display rules, updating registry/metadata together, regeneration/diff checks, and no false advertising of old versions.
2. Body's leading block set adds List/Table.
3. The obsolete unsupported-list/table sentence is replaced by the flat-list and explicit-header GFM-table contracts. The existing unsupported Parallel/image/reference/inline Anchor statement is retained with its narrowed list. List explanation stays in the same paragraph as Body/RawCode, matching the Markdown paragraph; Table and remaining-unsupported each get their own paragraph.

All order, limits and rejection conditions are retained: nonempty lists; exactly one Paragraph per item; checkbox and unmarked distinction; ordered start 0 through 999999999 and identical markers; no numeric clamping/increment overflow; marker-width continuation indent; adjacent lists rejected; ordinary checkbox-like text escaped. Tables retain explicit nonempty columns/header, header-only positive, row/cell order/count/alignment, empty Sentence cells only, shared inline behavior, exactly one extra pipe escape consumed by GFM, existing backslash/backtick preservation, and rejected Break/outer whitespace/multiple-block shapes. The GFM link target and label are preserved as a typed External link.

Ordinary statements are sentence literals. The renderer code and GFM link use explicit Sentence/Inline constructors. No new translation was invented. Ruby bases contain Kanji only; readings were manually chosen, including 非空/ひくう, 開始値/かいしち, 継続行/けいぞくぎょう, 平坦化/へいたんか, 昇格/しょうかく, 黙殺/もくさつ. 送り仮名 remains Text (引き継ぐ, 丸める, 委ねる, 区切り).

Checks: `check.py` parses the complete draft using existing `tools.audit.structure` formal forms (not production runtime), validates Ruby bases and absence of unannotated Kanji in the affected section, compares all ten section paragraphs' base text with the source, checks the exact External URL, verifies source bytes unchanged, and proves only three old lines are replaced while all unrelated lines retain exact bytes. The source comparison explicitly preserves two pre-existing inline-code spaces at soft-wrap boundaries; the initial strict comparison detected these existing differences, and they were not edited. UTF-8 without BOM and LF, plus scoped `git diff --check`, pass.

One initial author typo used `external-target`; reading the actual form definition showed the head is `external`. It was corrected before the formal structure check; no parser/runtime defect is claimed. No webpage fetch/reachability check, GitHub rendering, or independent semantic review was run by this author.
